=== OUTPUT ===
## 1. Contact and institution facts

**Determination:** **Yes, Franklin Ard is currently relevant for exploratory outreach about academic coaching and student-success workflows.** He is not verified as the economic, technical, or compliance buyer.

- **Current role:** Kennesaw State’s current staff page identifies him as Executive Director for Academic Coaching and Support. It says he leads academic-success initiatives and entered that executive-director role in May 2024. ([campus.kennesaw.edu](https://campus.kennesaw.edu/faculty-staff/academic-affairs/student-success/programs/about/meet-staff.php))
- **Unit:** Academic Affairs, Academic Coaching and Support.
- **Reporting line:** Not explicitly documented. Lori Lowder is Associate Vice Provost for Student Success, while Sheb True’s portfolio includes Student Success. Franklin’s direct supervisor remains unverified. ([kennesaw.edu](https://www.kennesaw.edu/academic-affairs/about/provosts-leadership-team/))
- **Institution:** Public, four-year university with 51,375 students in fall 2025, including 15,648 part-time students. ([campus.kennesaw.edu](https://campus.kennesaw.edu/offices-services/data-strategy/institutional-research/publications/common-data-set/cds-2025-2026.php))
- **Relevant institutional priority:** KSU’s strategic plan calls for stronger undergraduate retention, better outcomes in high-enrollment courses, and expanded student-success infrastructure. ([kennesaw.edu](https://www.kennesaw.edu/president/strategic-plan/create-learning-environment-where-students-thrive.php))
- **Documented systems:** Navigate360 supports undergraduate advising; Banner is the Student Information System; D2L Brightspace is the Learning Management System. ([campus.kennesaw.edu](https://campus.kennesaw.edu/current-students/academics/academic-advising/get-academic-advising/schedule-advising-eab.php))

**Motion assessment:** **M3 Student Success / Retention** is the best-supported hypothesis. M2 Attendance & Evidence is secondary but currently lacks a verified attendance-evidence problem.

